		{"id":"8004f8cbdb426a7d","type":"text","text":"## Introduction\n\n**Project Next Steps**\n- Writing based on prompt questions (flowers)\n\t- Exploring core concepts related to regenerative tech (use AI for speed)\n\t- Analyzing tools & case studies\n- Visualized ideas that fit into each provocation  (fruits)","x":-440,"y":-30,"width":362,"height":389,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"9b667841be11b4f6","type":"text","text":"## Trunks\n- Culture\n\t- Defining ourselves\n\t- Mediating our relationship to other humans\n\t- Mediating our relationship with the earth\n- Governance\n\t- Defining what to measure\n\t- Knowing what is true\n\t- Deciding on how to act\n\t- Who has the right to make these decisions\n- Economy\n\t- Deciding what to make, for who and how","x":-440,"y":391,"width":362,"height":524},
		{"id":"0d65e2de916d1ae7","type":"text","text":"## Ideas = Fruits","x":760,"y":720,"width":362,"height":389},
		{"id":"d677154c09ce6695","type":"text","text":"Concepts = Public Goods Funding","x":-440,"y":1019,"width":362,"height":60,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"b247d992bf2d8f39","type":"text","text":"Mechanisms = Quadratic Funding","x":-440,"y":1079,"width":362,"height":60,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"83d7ea044cb98171","type":"text","text":"Tools = Gitcoin","x":-440,"y":1139,"width":362,"height":60,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"4b5087036d18fc5e","type":"text","text":"## Responses = Flowers\n\n**What are our tools of self definition in relationship to others and the material world?**\n**How does our definition of ourselves guide our actions towards the world?**\n**How do we guide our beliefs and actions?**\n**How do we build the tools we use to act on the world?**\n**How do we define metrics that reflect life?**\n**How do we measure beyond markets**?\n**How do we include all voices, human & more-than human?**\n**How do we create narratives/maps?**\n**How do we know what is true?**\n**Who has the right & responsibility to make decide what is true?**\n**How do we turn data into meaning & maps?**\n**How do we make the right decisions?**\n**How do know what should be made and for who and how? \nHow do we ensure everyone's needs are addressed?\n\n","x":760,"y":-30,"width":362,"height":715},
		{"id":"9badd66c07920429","type":"text","text":"- Economic Tools\n    - Markets\n    - Money\n    - Community Currencies\n    - Hypercerts\n    - Tokens\n    - Hyperstructures?\n    - Gifting\n    - Supply Chain Tracking\n    - Quadratic Funding\n- Placemaking Tools\n    - Stories of Place\n    - Funnels\n    - Open Environments\n    - Public Squares\n- Sensemaking Tools\n    - Metrics\n    - Futures Thinking\n    - Imagination Infrastructure\n    - AI\n    - AI Sunflower\n    - Contextualization Engines\n    - Worldbuilding\n- Identity & Communication Tools\n    - Social Media\n    - Passports\n    - Soulbound\n    - Language\n    - Memes\n    - Mass Media\n    - Art\n    - Music\n    - Schools\n    - Relationship-Based Journalism\n- Governance Tools\n    - Representative Democracy\n    - Bioregional Gov\n    - Citizen’s Assemblies\n    - Laws\n    - Commons Gov\n    - DAOs\n    - Self-Sovereignity\n    - Nepalese Forests\n    - Guayana Indigenous Drones\n- Dark Matter\n- ReFi & DeFi\n- Social Media\n- Radar.xyz\n- Polis","x":322,"y":-30,"width":362,"height":1350,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"6807d82ca6afcdad","type":"text","text":"## Responses = Flowers\n\n- Why do we need regenerative information technology?\n\t- What is regenerative information technology?\n\t- Do we really need more technology to address climate change?\n\t- How do we create regenerative information technology? (Principles)\n- How might we create tools that allow us to define ourselves in relationship to others in a regenerative way?\n\t- What does it mean to define ourselves in relationship to others? (human & more-than-human)\n\t- How does our definition of ourselves guide our actions towards others?\n\t- What are our current tools of self definition in relationship to others?\n\t- What are some tools that are already supporting regenerative relationships?\n- How do we make decisions that align with our values and beliefs?\n\t- How do we define our values and beliefs?\n\t- How do our values & beliefs change over time? How do we allow \"good\" values and beliefs to surface?\n\t- How do we define what to measure or \"see\"?\n\t- How do we sense, measure or see? What tools do we use to support this?\n\t- How do we know what is true? How do we turn data into knowledge? How do we create narratives/maps?\n\t- How do we build collective intelligence? What does it mean to build collective intelligence?\n\t- What voices do we take into account and how?\n\t- How do we apply these values and beliefs to decision-making?\n\t- How do we make rules for behavior that align with those values, beliefs and knowledge?\n- How do we ensure everyone's needs are met?\n\t- How do know what should be made and for who and how? What is the role of markets and money?\n\t- How do we fund the things we need and want in the long-term?\n\t- How do we ensure externalities are internalized?\n\t- What does it mean to have ownership?\n\t- How do we reward people for their work and effort? How do we incentivize people to do the right things?\n\n","x":1180,"y":-30,"width":660,"height":1139,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"933f0bb0ab357cfa","type":"text","text":"**Questions to explore within the context of regenerative information technology**","x":1180,"y":-120,"width":660,"height":60},
		{"id":"86ed7abf7be2852e","type":"text","text":"## Core Concepts, Mechanisms & Tools = Leaves \n\n- Ecocultures\n- Monocultures\n- Evolution\n- Diversity\n- Emergence\n- Complexity\n- Psychetech = Infotech\n- Cultural Colonialism\n- Values\n- Value\n- Biophillic\n- Biomimetic\n- Intelligence\n- Collective Intelligence\n- Consciousness\n- Observation\n- Sensing\n- Sensemaking\n- Learning\n- Ring of Power x 6\n- Closed Loop Economies\n- Ownership = Cooperative Ownership\n- Investment = Regenerative Investment\n- Business = Regenerative Business\n- Capital = Multiple Forms of Capital\n- Love\n- Permission\n- Commons & Public Goods\n- Governance\n- Place\n- Placemaking (Reciprocal)\n- Time\n- Data & Information\n- Community\n- Identity\n- Indigenaity\n- Capture\n- Monopoly\n- Plurality\n- Care\n- Empathy","x":-40,"y":-30,"width":362,"height":1350,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"3901530cfbdce8c6","type":"text","text":"## Principles\n- Evolution as Sensemaking\n- Diversity\n- Emergence\n- Complexity\n- Values\n- Value\n- Biophillic\n- Biomimetic\n- Collective / Cooperative\n- Observation\n- Regeneration\n- Love\n- Plurality\n- Care\n- Empathy","x":1880,"y":-30,"width":362,"height":1350,"color":"6"}
